  "correct": "1",
  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\n(1st number + 2) = 2nd number,\n\n(2nd number + 2) = 3rd number.\n\nNow,\n\n(16, 18, 20)\n\n⇒ (16 + 2) = 18,\n\n⇒ (18 + 2) = 20.\n\nFor (17, 19, 21)\n\n⇒ (17 + 2) = 19,\n\n⇒ (19 + 2) = 21.\n\nNow, checking the options:\n\n**Option 1: (64, 66, 68)**\n\n**⇒ (64 + 2) = 66,**\n\n**⇒ (66 + 2) = 68.**\n\nOption 2: (24, 26, 30)\n\n⇒ (24 + 2) = 26,\n\n⇒ (26 + 2) = 28 ≠ 30.\n\nOption 3: (28, 30, 26)\n\n⇒ (28 + 2) = 30,\n\n⇒ (30 + 2) = 32 ≠ 26.\n\nOption 4: (36, 40, 42)\n\n⇒ (36 + 2) = 38 ≠ 40,\n\n⇒ (40 + 2) = 42.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option 1\".",
